  "verbalization": "Duvoglustat appears to interact with Cyclin-dependent kinase 2/cyclin E through a shared pathway involving 1-deoxymannojirimycin, which acts as a target of multiple enzymes. The evidence suggests that Duvoglustat may target a kinase-related protein, which in turn is inhibited by 1-deoxymannojirimycin, ultimately leading to the inhibition of Cyclin-dependent kinase 2/cyclin E. This mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple indirect pathways, all of which converge on 1-deoxymannojirimycin as a common mediator. The integration of these paths highlights a potential regulatory role for Duvoglustat in modulating kinase activity, possibly through the inhibition of 1-deoxymannojirimycin or through direct interaction with the target kinase. The evidence supports a mechanism where Duvoglustat may influence the activity of cyclin-dependent kinases by interacting with a downstream target, which is then inhibited by 1-deoxymannojirimycin, thereby affecting the phosphorylation and activity of Cyclin-dependent kinase 2/cyclin E.",
